.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt NOISY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noisy
.Nd crawl randomly selected HTTP and HTTPS links
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Op Fl l Ar level | Fl \-log Ar level
.Fl c Ar file | Fl \-config Ar file
.Op Fl t Ar seconds | Fl \-timeout Ar seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
repeatedly selects a root URL from its JSON configuration, fetches the page,
and randomly follows links found in quoted
.Sy href
attributes.
Only HTTP and HTTPS URLs are accepted, including redirect destinations.
DNS queries occur only as a side effect of resolving hostnames;
.Nm
does not generate independent DNS traffic.
.Pp
The configured depth limits linked-page visits after each root page.
After a successful linked-page request,
.Nm
waits for a random whole number of seconds greater than or equal to
.Ic min_sleep
and less than
.Ic max_sleep .
A failed linked-page request or a page with fewer than two accepted links is
added to the in-memory blacklist.
HTTP error status codes do not by themselves make a request fail; links in
their response bodies may still be used.
.Pp
Requests use a randomly selected configured user agent.
Each transfer has a five-second maximum, shortened when necessary by the
remaining overall timeout.
The overall timeout also limits waits between requests.
The process runs until that timeout expires or it receives
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGTERM .
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The file specified by
.Fl c
must be a JSON object containing the following keys:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic max_depth
Nonnegative integer.
Maximum number of linked-page visits after fetching a
root page.
.It Ic min_sleep
Nonnegative integer number of seconds for the lower end of the delay range.
.It Ic max_sleep
Integer greater than
.Ic min_sleep .
This value is an exclusive upper bound for the random delay.
.It Ic timeout
Either the JSON value
.Ql false
to disable the overall timeout, or a nonnegative integer number of seconds.
.It Ic root_urls
Nonempty array of HTTP or HTTPS URL strings.
One is selected at random for
each crawl cycle.
.It Ic blacklisted_urls
Array of strings.
A URL is rejected when it contains any entry as a
case-sensitive substring.
URLs of failed or dead-end linked pages are added
to this list in memory for the current process.
.It Ic user_agents
Nonempty array of user-agent strings.
One is selected for each request.
.El
.Pp
For example, see
.Pa config.json
in the source distribution.
.Sh OPTIONS
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file , Fl \-config Ar file
Read configuration from
.Ar file .
This option is required.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print usage information and exit successfully.
.It Fl l Ar level , Fl \-log Ar level
Set the minimum log level to
.Cm debug ,
.Cm info ,
.Cm warning ,
.Cm error ,
or
.Cm critical .
The default is
.Cm info .
.It Fl t Ar seconds , Fl \-timeout Ar seconds
Override the configured overall timeout when
.Ar seconds
is nonzero.
A value of zero leaves the configuration value unchanged.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Nm
uses libcurl for transfers.
Proxy environment variables supported by
libcurl, including
.Ev http_proxy ,
.Ev https_proxy ,
.Ev all_proxy ,
and
.Ev no_proxy ,
may affect requests.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa config.json
Example configuration in the source checkout.
.It Pa /opt/noisy/config.json
Configuration path used by the example service files.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors return status 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run using the configuration in the current directory:
.Pp
.Dl noisy --config config.json
.Pp
Run for one hour with debug logging:
.Pp
.Dl noisy -c /opt/noisy/config.json -l debug -t 3600
.Pp
Install the executable and manual page under the default
.Pa /usr/local
prefix:
.Pp
.Dl make install
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://curl.se/libcurl/c/ "libcurl documentation"
.Lk https://man.openbsd.org/mdoc.7 "mdoc(7)"
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
is a C fork of the Python program
.Lk https://github.com/1tayH/noisy 1tayH/noisy .
The C port is intended to reduce runtime overhead and improve reliability
when run as a long-lived service.
.Sh AUTHORS
The original program was written by
.An Itay Hury .
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
requests links found in fetched pages, including loopback and private-network
addresses.
Only use root URLs you trust, and apply network-level egress restrictions if
the process must not contact local or internal services.
